{"metadata":{"title":"Trie","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/Trie.swift#L26","fileName":"Trie.swift"},"externalID":"s:5Tries4TrieV"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"title":"Sets of sequences","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are sequences of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, stored as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the same words scalar by scalar, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" byte strings. Lookup,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"text":") for a key of ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":" symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}